  "body": "# Incorrect tuple destructuring in RiskEngine.twapEMA produces wrong TWAP\n- Severity: High\n\n## Targets\n- `RiskEngine.twapEMA`\n- `OraclePack.getEMAs`\n\n## Summary\n\n`RiskEngine.twapEMA` destructures the tuple returned by `oraclePack.getEMAs()` in the wrong order. `getEMAs()` returns `(spotEMA, fastEMA, slowEMA, eonsEMA, medianTick)`, but `twapEMA` binds the first three values as `(eonsEMA, slowEMA, fastEMA, , )`. This swaps the EMA components and drops the real eons EMA, producing an incorrect time-weighted price signal.\n\n## Vulnerability details\n\n`OraclePack.getEMAs()` returns (in-order):\n- `spotEMA`\n- `fastEMA`\n- `slowEMA`\n- `eonsEMA`\n- `medianTick`\n\nBut `twapEMA` does:\n- `eonsEMA <- spotEMA`\n- `slowEMA <- fastEMA`\n- `fastEMA <- slowEMA`\n- (drops the real `eonsEMA`)\n\nThe returned blended tick is therefore effectively computed from the wrong inputs.\n\n## Code references (original)\n\n- Wrong destructuring in `twapEMA`: [contracts/RiskEngine.sol](../contracts/RiskEngine.sol#L836-L841)\n- Correct return order in `getEMAs`: [contracts/types/OraclePack.sol](../contracts/types/OraclePack.sol#L210-L223)\n\n## Root cause\n\nFragile positional tuple destructuring: the caller assumes a different return order than the callee.\n\n## Impact\n\nHigh — `twapEMA` returns an incorrect price signal. Any downstream component using this TWAP for pricing, risk, margin, safe-mode gating, or liquidation decisions can be distorted. This can lead to mispriced risk, wrongful liquidations, missed liquidations, or systemic solvency issues.\n\n## Recommendation\n\n- Fix the tuple destructuring to match `getEMAs()`’s return order.\n- Add a unit test that constructs an OraclePack with distinct EMA values (spot != fast != slow != eons) and asserts the expected 60/30/10 weighted blend uses `(fast, slow, eons)`.\n\n## Reproduction (Foundry)\n\nQuick repro:\n\n- `forge test --match-path test/foundry/findings/CodeInspectionPoCs.t.sol --match-test test_PoC_twapEMA_tupleDestructuring_swapsEMAs -vvv`\n\nFallback (if `forge` tries to instantiate a forked environment locally):\n\n- Terminal 1: `anvil --port 8545 --silent`\n- Terminal 2: `FOUNDRY_ETH_RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8545 forge test --match-path test/foundry/findings/CodeInspectionPoCs.t.sol --match-test test_PoC_twapEMA_tupleDestructuring_swapsEMAs -vvv`",
  "proof_of_concept": "// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {ClonesWithImmutableArgs} from \"clones-with-immutable-args/ClonesWithImmutableArgs.sol\";\n\nimport {CollateralTracker} from \"@contracts/CollateralTracker.sol\";\nimport {RiskEngine} from \"@contracts/RiskEngine.sol\";\n\nimport {PanopticMath} from \"@libraries/PanopticMath.sol\";\n\nimport {LeftRightSigned} from \"@types/LeftRight.sol\";\nimport {MarketState, MarketStateLibrary} from \"@types/MarketState.sol\";\nimport {OraclePack, OraclePackLibrary} from \"@types/OraclePack.sol\";\nimport {TokenId} from \"@types/TokenId.sol\";\n\ncontract PanopticPoolMock {\n    function numberOfLegs(address) external pure returns (uint256) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract RiskEngineRateMock {\n    function interestRate(uint256, MarketState) external pure returns (uint128) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    function updateInterestRate(uint256, MarketState marketState) external pure returns (uint128, uint256) {\n        return (0, marketState.rateAtTarget());\n    }\n}\n\ncontract CollateralTrackerInterestHarness is CollateralTracker {\n    constructor() CollateralTracker(10) {\n        bytes32 slot = keccak256(\"panoptic.utilization.snapshot\");\n        assembly {\n            tstore(slot, 0)\n        }\n    }\n\n    function mintShares(address owner, uint256 shares) external {\n        _mint(owner, shares);\n    }\n\n    function setInterestState(address owner, int128 netBorrows, int128 userBorrowIndex) external {\n        s_interestState[owner] = LeftRightSigned.wrap(0)\n            .addToRightSlot(userBorrowIndex)\n            .addToLeftSlot(netBorrows);\n    }\n\n    function getInterestState(address owner) external view returns (int128 netBorrows, int128 userBorrowIndex) {\n        LeftRightSigned st = s_interestState[owner];\n        return (st.leftSlot(), st.rightSlot());\n    }\n\n    function setMarketStateRaw(uint256 raw) external {\n        s_marketState = MarketState.wrap(raw);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract CodeInspectionPoCsTest is Test {\n    function _deployCollateral() internal returns (CollateralTrackerInterestHarness ct) {\n        PanopticPoolMock pool = new PanopticPoolMock();\n        RiskEngineRateMock riskEngine = new RiskEngineRateMock();\n\n        CollateralTrackerInterestHarness impl = new CollateralTrackerInterestHarness();\n\n        ct = CollateralTrackerInterestHarness(\n            ClonesWithImmutableArgs.clone2(\n                address(impl),\n                abi.encodePacked(\n                    address(pool), // panopticPool\n                    true, // underlyingIsToken0\n                    address(0x1111), // underlyingToken\n                    address(0x1111), // token0\n                    address(0x2222), // token1\n                    address(riskEngine), // riskEngine\n                    address(0), // no pool manager\n                    uint24(3000) // pool fee\n                )\n            )\n        );\n\n        ct.initialize();\n    }\n\n    function test_PoC_hasNoDuplicateTokenIds_missesLastElementDuplicate() public {\n        TokenId[] memory arr = new TokenId[](3);\n        arr[0] = TokenId.wrap(111);\n        arr[1] = TokenId.wrap(222);\n        arr[2] = TokenId.wrap(111);\n\n        bool ok = PanopticMath.hasNoDuplicateTokenIds(arr);\n        assertTrue(ok, \"duplicate involving last element should have been detected\");\n    }\n\n    function test_PoC_twapEMA_tupleDestructuring_swapsEMAs() public {\n        RiskEngine engine = new RiskEngine(1, 1, address(0), address(0));\n\n        int24 spot = 1;\n        int24 fast = 100;\n        int24 slow = 10;\n        int24 eons = 1000;\n\n        uint96 emas = OraclePackLibrary.packEMAs(spot, fast, slow, eons);\n        OraclePack pack = OraclePackLibrary.storeOraclePack(0, 0, emas, 0, 0, 0, 0);\n\n        int24 expectedCorrect = int24((6 * int256(fast) + 3 * int256(slow) + int256(eons)) / 10);\n        int24 actual = engine.twapEMA(pack);\n\n        int24 expectedBuggy = int24((6 * int256(slow) + 3 * int256(fast) + int256(spot)) / 10);\n        assertEq(actual, expectedBuggy, \"unexpected twapEMA output (buggy formula mismatch)\");\n        assertTrue(actual != expectedCorrect, \"twapEMA unexpectedly matches correct formula\");\n    }\n\n    function test_PoC_addRiskPartner_carryCorruptsStrike() public {\n        TokenId tokenId = TokenId.wrap(0);\n\n        tokenId = tokenId.addRiskPartner(3, 0);\n        assertEq(tokenId.strike(0), 0, \"precondition: strike should be 0\");\n\n        TokenId tokenId2 = tokenId.addRiskPartner(3, 0);\n\n        // 3 + 3 = 6 = 0b110 => carry sets bit (shift + 2), which is strike's LSB (shift + 12).\n        assertEq(tokenId2.riskPartner(0), 2, \"riskPartner slot unexpectedly unaffected by carry\");\n        assertEq(tokenId2.strike(0), 1, \"strike LSB should have been flipped by carry\");\n    }\n\n    function test_PoC_transfer_allowsMovingSharesWithNetBorrows() public {\n        CollateralTrackerInterestHarness ct = _deployCollateral();\n\n        address alice = address(0xA11CE);\n        address bob = address(0xB0B);\n\n        ct.mintShares(alice, 100);\n        ct.setInterestState(alice, int128(1), int128(1e18));\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        ct.transfer(bob, 100);\n\n        assertEq(ct.balanceOf(alice), 0, \"alice should have transferred all shares\");\n        assertEq(ct.balanceOf(bob), 100, \"bob should have received shares\");\n\n        (int128 netBorrows, ) = ct.getInterestState(alice);\n        assertEq(netBorrows, 1, \"netBorrows unexpectedly changed by transfer\");\n    }\n\n    function test_PoC_accrueInterest_insolvent_doesNotAdvanceUserIndex() public {\n        CollateralTrackerInterestHarness ct = _deployCollateral();\n\n        address alice = address(0xA11CE);\n\n        // Give alice minimal shares, but set netBorrows + index delta so owed interest is huge in shares terms.\n        ct.mintShares(alice, 1);\n\n        uint32 epoch = uint32(block.timestamp >> 2);\n        MarketState forcedState = MarketStateLibrary.storeMarketState(2e18, epoch, 0, 0);\n        ct.setMarketStateRaw(MarketState.unwrap(forcedState));\n\n        ct.setInterestState(alice, int128(1000), int128(1e18));\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        ct.accrueInterest();\n\n        (, int128 userIndexAfter1) = ct.getInterestState(alice);\n        assertEq(userIndexAfter1, int128(1e18), \"userBorrowIndex should remain stale after insolvency\");\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        ct.accrueInterest();\n\n        (, int128 userIndexAfter2) = ct.getInterestState(alice);\n        assertEq(userIndexAfter2, int128(1e18), \"userBorrowIndex should remain stale on repeated accrual\");\n    }\n}",
